# * amt: queries, which match postings by amount.
# See also query-sum.test, which uses the same argument syntax.
<
2026-01-05 trip
    assets:checking
    expenses:travel     100 EUR @ $1.10

2026-01-06 trip
    assets:checking
    expenses:travel     $30

2026-01-09 groceries
    assets:checking
    expenses:food       $150

# ** 1. Without a commodity symbol, postings in any commodity are compared.
$ hledger -f- reg expenses amt:'>50'
2026-01-05 trip                 expenses:travel            100 EUR       100 EUR
2026-01-09 groceries            expenses:food                 $150          $150
                                                                         100 EUR

# ** 2. With a commodity symbol, just the amounts in that commodity are compared.
$ hledger -f- reg expenses amt:'>$50'
2026-01-09 groceries            expenses:food                 $150          $150

# ** 3. The symbol can also be written after the number.
$ hledger -f- reg expenses amt:'<200 EUR'
2026-01-05 trip                 expenses:travel            100 EUR       100 EUR

# ** 4. A transaction matches if any of its postings do (here the inferred $-110).
$ hledger -f- print amt:'>$100' desc:trip
2026-01-05 trip
    assets:checking
    expenses:travel                              100 EUR @ $1.10

>=

# ** 5. A bad argument gives an error.
$ hledger -f- reg amt:'>1,000'
>2 /could not parse "amt:>1,000"/
>=1

# ** 6. With -B, cur: and amt: still match the original commodity and quantity, as with -V/-X.
<
commodity BBB ; lots:
account revenues:gains ; type: G

2026-01-01 buy
    assets:inv       10 AAA @ $5
    assets:cash

2026-01-01 buy
    assets:broker    10 BBB @ $10
    assets:cash

2026-01-02 buy
    assets:broker    10 BBB @ $20
    assets:cash

2026-02-01 sell from both lots
    assets:broker   -15 BBB @ $30
    assets:cash
    revenues:gains

$ hledger -f- reg assets:inv cur:AAA amt:10 -B
2026-01-01 buy                  assets:inv                     $50           $50

# ** 7. Likewise for lot postings, converted to their cost basis.
$ hledger -f- reg assets:broker cur:BBB amt:10 -B
2026-01-01 buy                  assets:broker                 $100          $100
2026-01-02 buy                  assets:broker                 $200          $300

# ** 8. Except that a sale from several lots, when lot detail is collapsed (without --lots),
# is matched as converted to cost (here $-200, not -15 BBB).
$ hledger -f- reg assets:broker cur:BBB -B
2026-01-01 buy                  assets:broker                 $100          $100
2026-01-02 buy                  assets:broker                 $200          $300

# ** 9. With --lots it is matched as written.
$ hledger -f- reg assets:broker cur:BBB amt:-5 -B --lots
2026-02-01 sell from both lots  ..:{2026-01-02, $20}         $-100         $-100
